Feature: Switches
  SE is the arm switch (channel 5). When you press it in, the autopilot arms the plane. When you
  let it out, the autopilot disarms it. The six buttons on the front of the radio are the mode
  switch. The radio mixes them into one channel (channel 8), and the autopilot divides the
  channel into six positions: each button is a flight mode. Button 1 is QHOVER, 2 is QLOITER,
  3 is FBWA, 4 is CRUISE, 5 is AUTO and 6 is QRTL. QLOITER is the hover mode that holds the
  plane at one place. CRUISE is forward flight.

  Expectation: The arm switch arms the vehicle
    Given the arm switch is off
    And the vehicle is disarmed
    When the arm switch is on
    Then the vehicle is armed

  Expectation: Taking the arm switch down disarms the vehicle
    Given the arm switch is on
    And the vehicle is armed
    When the arm switch is off
    Then the vehicle is disarmed

  Expectation: The mode switch picks the mode
    Given the mode switch is QHOVER
    When the mode switch is QLOITER
    Then the autopilot mode is QLOITER
